<title>FINLAND: FINNISH MAY TRADE SURPLUS UP TO FIM 4.67 BLN -NCB.</title>
<headline>FINNISH MAY TRADE SURPLUS UP TO FIM 4.67 BLN -NCB.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's trade surplus rose to 4.67 billion markka in May from 4.28 billion in April and from 4.17 billion in May last year, the National Customs Board (NCB) said in statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The NCB earlier reported a preliminary May trade surplus of 4.7 billion markka.</p>
<p>The value of exports rose three percent year-on-year in May while the value of imports was flat compared to May 1996, NCB said.  </p>
<p>Trade balance (million markka):</p>
<p>		  May '97  April '97     May '96</p>
<p> Exports	 16,657     18,207     16,184</p>
<p> Imports	 11,989     13,925     12,010</p>
<p> Balance	 +4,668     +4,282     +4,174</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
